        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Soaking the dates in boiling water and bicarbonate of soda is not optional -- it softens them completely and breaks down the fibres so they blend into the batter invisibly. The finished sponge should have no detectable date pieces, just a deep, caramel-like richness."
          }
        ]
      },
